  [38;5;153mDancing across the clear divide,[39m
  [38;5;153mPanes like tears of liquid glass,[39m
  [38;5;153mWeeping while the storm rages on.[39m

  [38;5;153mIn summer heat they glow like fire,[39m
  [38;5;153mAmber light through amber panes,[39m
  [38;5;153mCasting shadows long and deep,[39m
  [38;5;153mPainting rooms with golden hues.[39m

  [38;5;153mA child presses palms against the glass,[39m
  [38;5;153mFingers spread like starfish thin,[39m
  [38;5;153mTwo panes between the world and wish,[39m
  [38;5;153mYearning for what lies beyond.[39m

  [38;5;153mThe wind strikes hard but cannot break,[39m
  [38;5;153mThese patient soldiers stand their ground,[39m
  [38;5;153mDivided into grid and square,[39m
  [38;5;153mEach pane reflects the passing clouds.[39m

  [38;5;153mSimple silence, strong and clear,[39m
  [38;5;153mBoundaries that bind yet free,[39m
  [38;5;153mPanes of glass that hold the line,[39m
  [38;5;153mBetween the safe and the unknown.[39m

